{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the ערוב shall depart from Pharaoh, from his servants, and from his people, tomorrow.</b> Moses says to Pharaoh: in order that you not suppose about me that the deeds I do are done by stratagem and cunning, by the wisdom of the hours, and that you think I know the hour and the time when the plague is fit to be removed and now that time has arrived — therefore I extend for you the time of the plague's removal until tomorrow, just as you said to me regarding the plague of the frogs. And therefore Moses fixed for him a set time in the other plagues as well with the word 'tomorrow' (מחר), both for the removal of the plague and for its coming."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:06.976080254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}